@verbs cd pwd homedir paths
@tier coder
@title where you are in the file tree
@see update cominfo

Every file name you type that does not start with '/' or '~' is
read from the directory you are standing in.

  pwd

Says which directory that is.

  cd <directory>

Moves you there. '..' goes one up, and 'cd' with nothing takes you
back to your home directory. '~' is /home/<your name>/, always.

  cd <object>

Takes you to the directory of that object's file: 'cd here' lands
in the directory of the place you are in. Naming another creator
takes you to the directory they are in.

  homedir [<directory>]

Sets the directory you start in when you log on, and the one bare
'cd' returns to. With no argument it says which one it is.
